{"title":"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047bc14560bc613b17fb1ba735bba221764510a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> is a sequence of 0's and 1's. T is the number of triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec57565678fe2a4e713d421b45f511e3a537bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i, a_j, a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54db52274b430e27e179fe50ba07bd756c62c30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> which are not equal to (0, 1, 0) or (1, 0, 1). For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3c0e0875b8695a1e1e2bb48d8c5e73c4e5245f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74efea4ce02738f0765b2b9d578ceb427631eadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49e4f75f0ae44fe7e6a0aef69211da14d9f872a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1645d206c02ab33bad7aa9263e9f74565fb56bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> plus the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248ee41acf29d8dac6d244350970db2cb67e3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173cd3fdd338d6b92a0345a0fcd03ec9ec36f405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j\\neq a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0f058c03926379f034c1605752dea00c0d908a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)\\cdot\\left(\\frac{f(i)-1}2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"199\" height=\"48\" />. If n is odd, what is the smallest value of T?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5664e459e69ad5aba16308c5737d5359a91668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49e4f75f0ae44fe7e6a0aef69211da14d9f872a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1645d206c02ab33bad7aa9263e9f74565fb56bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07ccde14bf8f9909e2dffb32cc376e7d334db58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248ee41acf29d8dac6d244350970db2cb67e3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173cd3fdd338d6b92a0345a0fcd03ec9ec36f405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j\\neq a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee94c8d5861882df2d8583d1e60774f1745ce97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i) = g(i) + h(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d2502637390a05115b444abcf10e1525a8e9d09b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(i)\\left(\\frac{f(i)-1}2\\right) = (g(i)+h(i))\\left(\\frac{g(i)+h(i)-1}2\\right)\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c4981e31defd3d3012b9c7b9b21eb6fbd2e26c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{g(i)^2+h(i)^2+2g(i)h(i)-g(i)-h(i)}{2}\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/0561f9e22fe9af4ddb0ab256a28572f9a3362a14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{g(i)(g(i)-1)}{2} + \\frac{h(i)(h(i)-1)}{2} + g(i)h(i)\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b7ea4ae6d15a9517db6e09c0f6ec28b94be4c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{g(i)}{2} + \\binom{h(i)}{2} + \\binom{g(i)}{1}\\binom{h(i)}{1}\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>The first term counts the number of triples of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f36b13a11a14accae8e072c0cf34d69267bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d43e6e252922c8df825114d48e1418c7516d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> as the last member. The second term counts the number of triples of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4b3b309891ebb408b38b99d65c87d869d4f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10e4a7cc979f7d958177f48e71c33f4f908c116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> as the first member. The third term counts the number of triples of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/96521b1a203c3bb20a336e59cb63b1f0d232fb63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/992be26a8d2b207f24cef4a13386cda421e070d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> as the middle member. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d2051b9c69eb0ff9b0ef253ecd03e373e74247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)\\cdot\\left(\\frac{f(i)-1}2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"168\" height=\"53\" /> exhaustively and uniquely counts all triples except for those of the forms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb469a4813ba1cc1aae00e5d449f3bfa0c344f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8530c391dbd145877d3fad6e5208f3c6ca98a1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFinding the smallest value of T is trickier. First, consider what happens when we reverse the order of the sequence. For a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, the less than/greater than relation between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, which determines whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> counts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/eda8881f130a4e10be6eab9663cb6526ed1bf3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i = a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/8085cdfc632da84dc46bbbfaab2e7e0459f54acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\neq a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" />, is reversed for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743293b410b7d3bdf6a048265134ab7aa60b38b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\neq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />, so in the new sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> will correspond to a function value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e67f872ebb59e6a6138489f8d61fd4d755fc6fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1-f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />. However, notice that T does not change when we reverse the order of the sequence, as any triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb469a4813ba1cc1aae00e5d449f3bfa0c344f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8530c391dbd145877d3fad6e5208f3c6ca98a1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> will also be present in the reversed sequence. We'll set T from the original sequence equal to T from the reversed sequence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083ef1548a70107157c4939e50ac32e63b16a357.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)(f(i)-1)) = \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^n (n-1-f(i))\\cdot\\left((n-2-f(i))\\right)\\]\" width=\"469\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423899857c3943eaf4847aecb07d204dde9499dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n(f(i)^2 - f(i)) = \\sum_{i=1}^n (n^2 - 2n -nf(i)-n+2+f(i)-nf(i)+2f(i)+f(i)^2)\\]\" width=\"552\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559da9e702da8d1f12bd401f3358083c0e40f83c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = \\sum_{i=1}^n ((3-2n)f(i)+n^2-3n+2)\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f988f7d5576a250ba7a34519399ca10b37d47fa3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = (3-2n)\\sum_{i=1}^n (f(i))+n^3-3n^2+2n\\]\" width=\"371\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0af6c3d12ca0ffffcbece4b8cceee60b8aa998f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = (3-2n)\\sum_{i=1}^n (f(i))+n(n-1)(n-2)\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e6550967ec07ead85daecec6d778cec2a9813c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2n-4)\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = n(n-1)(n-2)\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf6e453e5810c5cd41a9310b35357d0a875815c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>We find that for all sequences, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b50e63fdd174e3f80a927d06be217aa0aa937c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"157\" height=\"53\" />. We'll use the method of Lagrange multipliers to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9ed0228ad7283b110f34bd6a7fca6f727a5204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)(f(i)-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"155\" height=\"53\" /> subject to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b50e63fdd174e3f80a927d06be217aa0aa937c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i) = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"157\" height=\"53\" />. Note that this only establishes a sufficient condition for a minimum, we will show later that it is possible to define a sequence which satisfies that condition.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d177f6e1a6ab571e9116c5446b439c7476e9f4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathcal{L} (f(1),...,f(n), \\lambda) = \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)(f(i)-1) + \\lambda\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n(f(i))-\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"535\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14495e04cc2d09f6be2c9782883bc1c8fc331f31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d\\mathcal{L}}{df(i)} = \\frac{1}{2}(2f(i)-1) + \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"199\" height=\"44\" />. Setting the gradient to 0 and solving quickly yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3aaf573e58fc11bbc3d975836c41471a01c8097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i) = \\frac{1}{2}-\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />. Then we take the derivative with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e07b94d697271ebbc699e16506aa4fb02113ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d\\mathcal{L}}{d\\lambda} = \\sum_{i=1}^n (f(i)) - \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"217\" height=\"53\" />. Setting the gradient to 0 and substituting our expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74efea4ce02738f0765b2b9d578ceb427631eadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf52c38ef78165195c64aaf8aef19e47d8f589c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = n(\\frac{1}{2}-\\lambda) - \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"40\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334cef6b290929041efeb1018f7d0c509f103dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda = \\frac{2-n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. Finally, substituting this back into the expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74efea4ce02738f0765b2b9d578ceb427631eadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a867b4047d7b810d89477d94898a65293fcb5dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i) = \\frac{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nThis tells us that if we can define a sequence for any odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a867b4047d7b810d89477d94898a65293fcb5dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i) = \\frac{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, this would certainly be a sequence which minimizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. In fact, an alternating sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b893ca458aa5d78db1f5149cc7ae3d320949a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1,0,1,...,0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" /> satisfies this, because for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49e4f75f0ae44fe7e6a0aef69211da14d9f872a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1645d206c02ab33bad7aa9263e9f74565fb56bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14d5f0444513259fed3587fa864474907cea232b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{i-1}{2} \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" /> and the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248ee41acf29d8dac6d244350970db2cb67e3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />  such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e4095332688df870bdcc82e5afbaa7e25338250d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j \\neq a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1917b8ffc3ea5cc8d8380d997deacfb70c773cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil \\frac{n-i}{2} \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"39\" />. For odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4f278c6d6e09a1483d52e415bdfa0211ad4da02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{i-1}{2} \\rfloor + \\lceil \\frac{n-i}{2} \\rceil = \\frac{i-1}{2} + \\frac{n-i}{2} = \\frac{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"343\" height=\"39\" /> and for even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3c4a2ebca657e30b10d69fdea6145fc5c79674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{i-1}{2} \\rfloor + \\lceil \\frac{n-i}{2} \\rceil = \\frac{i-2}{2} + \\frac{n-i+1}{2} = \\frac{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"374\" height=\"39\" />. \nThus T is minimized by this alternating sequence, where it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689af53c685a19e8afc4e7f4905ca5472393b918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n \\frac{n-1}{2} \\frac{n-3}{4} = \\frac{n(n-1)(n-3)}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"275\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO\" title=\"1987 USAMO\">1987 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p